# Supabase Migrations

## Source of truth
- All schema changes MUST be new numbered files in `supabase/migrations/` (e.g. `003_add_notes.sql`)
- Never apply schema changes only in Supabase Dashboard without a matching migration file
- Migration files are committed to git — they are the blueprint for new environments

## After creating or editing a migration
Always remind the user at the end of your response:

1. Run `npm run db:push` to apply pending migrations to the linked Supabase project
2. Run `npm run db:status` if unsure which migrations are applied locally vs remote

## If push fails with "already exists"
The object exists in the DB but migration history is missing (usually from manual SQL Editor runs). Fix with:

```bash
supabase migration repair <version> --status applied --linked
npm run db:push
```

Do NOT re-run SQL that creates objects already in the database.

## New migration checklist
- [ ] File named `NNN_descriptive_name.sql` (sequential number)
- [ ] RLS enabled on any new table + `firm_id` column
- [ ] Update `types/index.ts` if schema types changed
- [ ] Remind user to `npm run db:push`
